    "title": "SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket launches Starlink satellites from Vandenberg, CA Space Force Base",
    "text": "Ringer's Roller Rink is coming to Seaport Village this summer, offering public skating 365 days a year, steps from the Embarcadero. SAN DIEGO — Seaport Village is getting a new waterfront tenant this summer, and it is bringing nostalgia on wheels. Ringer's Roller Rink, which already operates a location on Federal Boulevard in southeast San Diego, is set to open a second rink in the heart of Seaport Village, just south of Kettner Boulevard in the former Indian Trails space, between Bay Company Souvenirs and the soon-to-open Cork and Batter. Owner and CEO Nili \"Ringer\" Goldfarb said she knew the waterfront location was right the moment she saw it. \"The energy is right. It's going to be such an awesome addition to Seaport Village,\" Goldfarb said. The new rink will feature a smooth concrete oval accommodating up to 50 skaters at a time, a concession stand serving Dippin' Dots and other snacks, a souvenir and gear shop, and skate rentals in all sizes. Admission starts at $18. Goldfarb, a former competitive roller derby player, opened the Federal Boulevard location in early 2020, just before the pandemic. After a difficult start, she rebranded under the Ringer's name and built a loyal following. She said Southern California has always had a deep connection to outdoor skating. \"There are always some of us that are holding down the fort for roller skating, and especially here in San Diego and in Southern California, there is a long history of beach and outdoor roller skating here,\" Goldfarb said. Seaport Village draws roughly 4 million visitors a year and has been working to attract new tenants and restaurants to revitalize the waterfront shopping center. Visitors and locals alike said they are excited about the addition. \"Bring some energy down here and give people something to do that is nice, besides eat and drink,\" said San Diego resident Mike Calendar. The rink will be open 365 days a year for public skating, with private event rentals available on select dates. Goldfarb said the target opening is early June, though a firm date has not been set. \"We are pushing so hard for early June, but until we are all the way through the process, we won't have a true date,\" she said.",
